    "description": "Of all the warlords and heroes who swore to bring an end to Dong Zhuo's regime, Wang Kuang stood out for his aggression and drive. From Henei, he sought to cross the Yellow River and storm the tyrant's camps from the north, and from there be the first to enter the capital and receive rightful recognition for his deeds and loyalty. However, even his hasty mustering was too slow to prevent the despotic regent from setting the ancient city of Luoyang ablaze. All that awaited for him at Heyang Ford was a mighty army of hardened Xiliang warriors, and despite fightly bravely, Wang Kuang found himself routed. With his bridgehead over the river lost and his armies scattered, the courageous warlord limped back to Henei to lick his wounds. There, he cursed his coalition \"allies\" for their ineptitude and unwillingness to advance, blaming them entirely for his defeat. Now, with rage and a hint of paranoia bubbling within him, Wang Kuang seeks to rebuild his forces. This time, he will trust only his own strength and capabilities, even if it means eschewing diplomacy and striking out at his former friends...",
