    "adjective": "Liu Yao",
    "mode": "standard",
    "leader_template": "3k_main_template_historical_liu_yao_hero_earth",
    "subtitle": "Welcoming Magistrate",
    "description": "Being distantly related to the Imperial clan, Liu Yao has thus far lead a privileged and charmed life. A scholarly, kind and honourable man, he became famous as a youth for personally rescuing a kinsman who had been kidnapped by brigands and rogues. This act helped accelerate his political career and standing, allowing him to rapidly rise through the bureaucracy. Now, he has been appointed his first major political position - one that will take him far from the capital, which may be a blessing in disguise given recent events in Luoyang. His post in distant Danyang finds him surrounded by squabbling local officials, warlords taking advantage of weakening Imperial authority, bandits and Shanyue rebels. Although not a man with a love for war, Liu Yao must find a way to secure his position, lest he be swept aside by the tides. With clever use of diplomacy and the blade alike, an opportunity awaits him, the chance to unleash the full potential of the fertile but wild Jiangdong region. A prosperous future lies in store, for those swift and bold enough to take decisive action...",
