    "mode": "standard",
    "leader_template": "3k_main_template_historical_wang_lang_hero_earth",
    "subtitle": "Ardent Educator",
    "description": "One of the foremost men of learning of his era, Wang Lang was considered a prodigy of poetry and history from a very early age, with him especially noted for being a master of the Classics. He boasts a personal friendship with many other famous scholars, such as the likes of Tao Qian, Kong Rong and Hua Xin. Wang Lang fosters this academic background into his administration, promoting the construction of schools and providing tutors for the poor and needy. He uses his rhetoric and quick tongue to charm the local magnates, and conversely fiercely debates matters of law and legislature to those opposed to his policies. However, Wang Lang has now found himself in a world where rectitude and erudition cannot ensure either the stability of his government, nor his own survival. This notable scholar must learn new lessons, and fast, or a painful and miserable end to his governance sadly awaits.",
