    "leader_template": "3k_main_template_historical_kong_zhou_hero_water",
    "subtitle": "Pure Conversationalist",
    "description": "Famed under the Heavens for his mastery of philosophical debate and soothing sophistry, Kong Zhou understands well the importance of harmony and balance in all aspects of life. Fearing the dangers of allowing Dong Zhuo's cruel regime to bring instability to the realm, he eagerly answers the call of arms to depose the despot. From his position in Yuzhou, however, the court and imprisoned Emperor seem further and further away - especially after the old capital is set alight and the tyrant retreats far to the west. Kong Zhou also finds himself somewhat isolated from his coalition allies - but he is certain that with careful diplomacy and wise words, he can help direct his fellow patriots from afar. Yuzhou, however, is an unstable land surrounded by greedy foes. Should these rebels and caitiffs all about fail to listen to logic and reason, Kong Zhou realises a far firmer hand will be required to maintain the balance.",
