    "adjective": "Han Fu",
    "mode": "standard",
    "leader_template": "3k_main_template_historical_han_fu_hero_earth",
    "subtitle": "Diligent Agriculturalist",
    "description": "Soldiers cannot fight without equipment, and armies cannot march when hungry. Generals may win battles, but wars are fought with logistics. As the man responsible for supplying much of the northern warlords, Han Fu is keenly aware of his own importance. Even as the rest of the coalition dithers and falters before the tyrant, Han Fu slowly and calmly stockpiles his provisions. He knows keenly that the northern lords will be reliant on food grown on his lands for sustenance, and their own ambitions are all for naught if they cannot even feed their men. Therefore, Han Fu finds himself in an enviable position, one that can puppet the lords and generals with sacks of grain. Should he act with a keen mind and a bold strength of will, he has a prime opportunity to dominate the north through diplomacy and logistics alone, all the while his foes only get hungrier. He must be wary, however, not to overplay his hand too soon - starving wolves can act erratically, after all, and cannot be tamed.",
