    "description": "From the furthest western stretches of Liangzhou, Song Jian has been in open rebellion against the Han for years. One of the last remaining leaders of the original Liang Rebellion, he has remained steadfast and stubbornly independent, even isolating himself from his fellow rebels. All calls to submit or surrender fall on deaf ears, as he expands his domain to dominate the very sources of the great Yellow River. As he strives to dominate the western trade routes and the river sources, Song Jian is slowly amassing insurmountable wealth and power. With rivers of gold and silk running through his fingertips, and armies of loyal Qiang warriors at his side, it will be difficult indeed for any Han loyalist to dislodge the so-called Lord of the Sources...",
