                "title": "Imperial Favour",
                "description": "The emperor has been disappointed with your actions. He may choose to punish you.",
                "icon": "data/images/resources/3k_dlc07_imperial_favour.png",
                "bullets": [
                  "Satisfaction is how content a character is with their current faction and situation. If it falls too low, they may choose to leave.",
                  "Improved diplomatic relations will lead to better deals and less aggression from other factions.",
                  "Corruption is the loss of income due to the size of your realm to various, insalubrious elements of society."
                ],
                "effects": [
                  "Imperial favour defines how the emperor views you and your actions. To increase your favour, make sure that your faction has high public order and a food surplus. (faction-wide)",
                  "Your imperial favour is low. The emperor dislikes you and the actions you have taken so far. You must treat your own people and neighbours better if you don't want the emperor to take actions against you. (faction-wide)",
                  "Be careful when attacking armies belonging to Han factions or sacking and looting Han settlements, as your imperial favour will decrease. (faction-wide)"
                ]
