    "mode": "standard",
    "leader_template": "3k_main_template_historical_qiulijiu_hero_fire",
    "subtitle": "Leader of Five Thousand",
    "description": "A fierce leader of the Wuhuan peoples, the name of Qiuliju is feared across the northern steppes. His people once aided the Han as auxiliary cavalry, but angered over a lack of pay, they joined a rebellion lead by Zhang Ju and Zhang Chun against the Empire. After many devastating clashes with his nemesis Gongsun Zan and his famed White Riders, Qiulijiu's wrath was eventually pacified by the arrival of the princely Liu Yu. Being one of the scant few Han officials who had the respect of the Wuhuan tribes, Liu Yu was able to convince the enraged chieftains to turn their backs on the rebellion. Joining forces with Liu Yu, Qiuliju aided in the pacification of the region. However, his enmity for Gongsun Zan has not begun to quell, and his warriors hunger for greater things. With the Xianbei still broken and divided, the Wuhuan are in position to stake a claim for hegemony over the steppes. Right now, the soothing diplomacy and kindness of Liu Yu are the only things sparing the world Qiulijiu's rampage...",
