    "leader_template": "ironic_template_historical_handan_shang_hero_wood",
    "subtitle": "The Steadyhanded Prefect",
    "description": "The leaders of the Liang Rebels may have allegedly submitted to the court, but their armies remain, as do many of their Qiang allies. To the Han officials sent west to wrest control back of the troubled frontier province, their task is steep and unenviable. Handan Shang, a scholarly man of good stock, is one of the leading officials newly assigned to a post in this rebellious land. For now, he has little choice but to align himself with other court officers sent to Liangzhou, putting aside any personal grievances to become a leading figure amongst them. He must work swiftly to establish a foothold of control over the territory he has been assigned to govern, knowing full well that the court is far too preoccupied with other matters to send more help. Although some of the regional lords may be amiable to diplomacy or treaties, Handan Shang knows that trusting the likes of Han Sui or Song Jian is a foolish errand, and more secure means of deterrence will be required to quell their petty ambitions.",
