    "subtitle": "Rallier of Troops",
    "description": "The proud governor of the Yangzhou region, Chen Wen announces a call to arms of all the brave and stalwart warriors of his province, so that their homes may be protected from threats external and internal. His skill at mustering troops is matched only by his talent in forging diplomatic allegiances. Despite not being an official member of the great coalition to oppose the tyrant, he has supported several of the warlords by providing troops, supplies and officers. With the south of his sphere of influence, across the great river, divided into petty lords, bandits, Shanyue chieftains, rebels and minions of Dong Zhuo, Chen Wen must work tirelessly to reunify Yangzhou under his leadership. The closed fist and the open hand are options both available to him, and indeed, if he is to safeguard his future, both his blade and diplomacy must be wielded in concert.",
