    "leader_template": "3k_main_template_historical_bian_rang_hero_water",
    "subtitle": "Caustic Critic",
    "description": "A prolific writer, poet and historian, Bian Rang has served the Imperial court faithfully for many years. His vast volume of works have won him the admiration and respect of countless peers, including fellow renowned gentlemen such as Tao Qian. Following the commands of the late He Jin, Bian Rang accepted his current position as a regional governor without question. He has managed his lands ably and capably since arriving, and has used the opportunity to ever expand his portfolio of rhapsodies and poetry. However, Bian Rang is a man known very well for his almost blunt honesty and outspoken criticism of wrongdoers, criminals and the unfaithful. For that reason, it is little reason that he has refused to sworn loyalty to the despot that now holds his Imperial Majesty as a hostage in the distant western capital. The vile Dong Zhuo is not the only man who was earned the ire of Bian Rang, however. His keen gaze has turned to his neighbouring administrators and governors, too, carefully observing each of them for signs of warmongers, tyranny or abuse of their ambitions. Should any of them earn his emnity, Bian Rang will not be subtle with his criticisms, and will put his own life at risk if it means scolding them for evil deeds!",
