    "leader_template": "3k_main_template_historical_zhu_hao_hero_fire",
    "subtitle": "Unflappable Prefect",
    "description": "Being the son of the famed general Zhu Jun, even Zhu Hao's childhood was lived with military efficiency and strictness. The first books he learned to read were old army manuals, and he was soon directing his household servants around as if they were soldiers. Now, he finds himself promoted to the position of a local governor, down in the Jiangdong region where his father once earned his own fame. Zhu Hao has heavy expectations weighing down on him, and he is eager to both prove his capabilities and break out from the shadow of his famous father. Personally leading a handpicked militia of veterans, personal friends and recruited local warriors, Zhu Hao has made it his mission to decapitate the corrupt magnates who have used their wealth and fame to abuse the people for far too long. He sees potential enemies everywhere, but may have to learn to step out of the shoes of soldiery and venture into the world of diplomacy and politics as well, lest he anger one lord too many...",
