    "leader_template": "3k_main_template_historical_zhuge_xuan_hero_fire",
    "subtitle": "The Nurturer of Dragons",
    "description": "A dutiful and proud man, Zhuge Xuan is more passionate than most in his duties as administrator of Yuzhang. As well as striving hard to safeguard his territory from bandits, rebels and other threats, Zhuge Xuan believes he has a far more important mission that he must dutifully adhere to. The children of his late relative, Zhuge Gui, have been placed under his care, and it is these youths the represent the future of the entire Zhuge clan. Yuzhang is a land distant from the Central Plains and perhaps safe from the mayhem that has caused the north to shatter, but it is no tranquil island amidst a stormy sea. On the contrary, the Jiangdong region is home to countless perils, and as central authority has broken down, the lines between who governs what have blurred. Shanyue and brigands rise in rebellion, and local lords begin arming themselves and seeing to their own ambitions. Standing firm amidst all of this, Zhuge Xuan is akin to a beacon shining a light to the future. Even if it costs him his life, he will ensure that the Zhuge clan's next generations are positioned to make their mark on the world.",
