    "state_name": "Ma Ai",
    "adjective": "Ma Ai",
    "mode": "standard",
    "leader_template": "ironic_template_historical_ma_ai_hero_fire",
    "subtitle": "The Corridor's Warden",
    "description": "The matters of the Central Plains, the warlords, the rebellions and infighting, mean little to the likes of Ma Ai, a man sent to watch over the very gates to the Han's most extreme western borders. The concerns of his tenure thus far have been primarily securing the crucial trade routes west, and bartering and negotiating with foreign peoples across the frontier. However, as remote and distant his post may be, Ma Ai is not unaware of the dismal carnage that has erupted elsewhere in the Empire. With rebellions across Liangzhou, the once flowing rivers of gold and silk have practically dried up. Elsewhere, with the capital burning and the entire court uprooting, commerce has begun to collapse, especially as the Central Plains explode into petty clashing and skirmishes between rival clans. Therefore, perhaps in this trying times, even a practically forgotten border guard like Ma Ai must make a mark on the world? After all, what use is doggedly protecting a barren frontier when the heart of the Empire is being torn out? Although stalwartly looking out west as a watchman, Ma Ai keeps a single eye trained eastwards, in case his services and soldiers are required elsewhere...",
